# handwave

A board in a browser pane you draw on **while you are talking**. You keep
answering in chat; the board carries the boxes, arrows and keywords.

**Draw as you talk, not after.** A sentence, then the thing that sentence is
about, then the next sentence. Never build the whole diagram in one call — that
is a picture, and it loses the thread it was meant to carry.

## Commands

Run these in the terminal. The first one starts a board and prints its URL;
give the person that URL once, early.

```bash
handwave draw '{"op":"title","text":"Placing an order"}'
handwave open              # once, at the start: its own chromeless window
handwave draw '{"op":"node","id":"gw","kind":"gateway","label":"API Gateway","sub":"authn"}'
handwave draw '{"op":"edge","from":"gw","to":"orders","label":"gRPC"}'
handwave say  "The gateway does **authn** and rate limiting, then hands off."
handwave step 1            # light up one hop of the flow; also: step next / step off
handwave clear             # before a new, unrelated explanation
handwave snapshot -o docs/flow.html
```

## Ops

```jsonc
{"op":"node","id":"db","kind":"datastore","label":"Postgres","sub":"orders"}
{"op":"edge","from":"orders","to":"bus","label":"publish","async":true}   // async = dashed
{"op":"note","label":"idempotency key\nlives 24h"}                        // your own handwriting
{"op":"boundary","label":"our VPC","members":["gw","orders","db"]}
{"op":"step","edge":"gw>orders","step":"Gateway authenticates and forwards"}
{"op":"remove","id":"gw"}
```

Pass an array to draw several at once, when they are genuinely one thought.

`kind`: `client` `gateway` `service` `compute` `datastore` `cache` `queue`
`external` `note`. Each has its own drawing, and colour follows kind, so only
pass `body` when deliberately grouping across kinds.

You never place anything: columns come from the edges. Draw the node, then the
edge into it, and it lands where it belongs.

## Judgement

- A board earns its place or it does not get drawn. Don't redraw a list you
  just wrote.
- Eight or ten boxes is a board someone can hold in their head. Twenty is a map.
  Draw the part under discussion, not the system.
- Label every arrow (`gRPC`, `INSERT`, `publish`). An unlabelled arrow only says
  two things are connected.
- `sub` is for what changes the design (`3 replicas`, `idempotency`), not a
  restatement of the label.
- Redrawing an existing `id` updates it, so correcting the board out loud is
  cheap and normal.
